		(property "Note" "EN = DRV_EN, EN* = GND. DRV_EN is SB_PRSNT_IN through the FITTED link R_DRVEN_PRSNT, so the drivers run only while a powered, configured far end asserts presence: a radio on with the Tang off pushes no LVDS current into the dead Gowin. REQUIRES the sideband cable (CAB-8654/8654-8i-P); the no-sideband variant leaves the link dead. R_DRVEN_ON (not fitted) forces them on for bench tests."
			(at 467.36 356.87 0)
			(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes)))
		(property "Description" "Quad LVDS driver, 400 Mbps, SOIC-16. Channel 1 is the DUPLICATE forward clock, fed from the same translated net as the primary: the forward clock is the single point of failure for the whole receive path, the far end has spare pins and trains whichever lane works, and this costs one trace. Channels 2 and 3 are the auxiliary transmit pair, channel 4 is a spare driver channel with its input held low"
			(at 467.36 356.87 0)
			(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes)))
